:expect-pins 8
# Fresh-process temporal case TA-22.

# The worked family window derives reviewed-interval status; the raw date and order claims retain its boundaries.
? time(Window_Custody, ReviewedInterval).
# => TRUE

# An ordinary standing query remains bounded beside the temporal rules.
? person(Adam).
# => TRUE

# The exact opaque food entitlement executes directly against the full T3 source.
? entitled(Adam, event { eats() }).
# => TRUE

# An ordinary public-answerability query remains bounded beside the temporal rules.
? authority(Court).
# => TRUE

# The bounded case gate still derives the expected current custody result.
? prisoner(Adam).
# => TRUE

# Recognition remains a separate unread conclusion.
? reward(Quin).
# => TRUE

# Severity remains a placement input, not a duration input.
? severe(Lalo).
# => TRUE

# The case-renewal depends on reviewed case/time evidence rather than recognition or severity.
? correct(Case_Adam, ActivePower).
# => TRUE
